      "heading": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test",
      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "CAD and drafting skills lead to careers in mechanical, civil, electrical, architectural and product drawing, where employers expect accurate drawings to standard, clean files, and the ability to follow a markup from an engineer or architect without confusion."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Choose a discipline, learn one drafting tool well, practise drawing to standard and build a drawing set that shows dimensions, notes and revision control."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Check employer requirements and use legitimate student or trial licences."
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "proof",
      "title": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test"
